If you want it like you wrote it, you need

idx.na <http://idx.na> = rep(NA, n)
traffic1 = 1:n
traffic2 = n + 1:n
traffic3 = 2*n + 1:n

... f(idx.na <http://idx.na>, model="iid",values=1:(3*n)) +
    f(traffic1, b1, copy="idx.na <http://idx.na>") +
    f(traffic2, b2, copy="idx.na <http://idx.na>") +
    f(traffic3, b3, copy="idx.na <http://idx.na>") +	 ...

the first 'f()' defines the random effects, with length 3*n, but since
idx.na <http://idx.na> are all NA, its not in use.

the other ones, uses the correct part of the random effect with weights
b2, say (I guess b2 is a vector),

please check it out first on a simulated example

H

